<title>USA: Ingersoll-Rand ups div after 3-for-2 split.</title>
<headline>Ingersoll-Rand ups div after 3-for-2 split.</headline>
<dateline>WOODCLIFF LAKE, N.J. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingersoll-Rand Co said Wednesday that it is splitting its stock 3-for-2, and raising its regular quarterly dividend on the post-split shares.</p>
<p>Ingersoll-Rand said that the quarterly dividend will be $0.15 on the post-split shares, versus $0.205 on the pre-split shares, a 9.8 percent increase in the dividend rate.</p>
<p>The company said the split will be in the form of a stock dividend, payable, along with the higher dividend, on September 2, to shareholders of record August 19.</p>
